    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The inference rule is an unrestricted predicate on the complete table of outputs for all finite input histories. This captures the author's stipulation about unbounded evidence, but agreement with such a predicate does not imply that a verdict can be obtained by a physical measurement of the kind discussed in P-D53."
